WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.919
Well, there's a new horror movie trailer out
for the first time in a while, so just for

00:00:03.919 --> 00:00:08.430
old times' sake: if you want to hear the meaning
behind this, then stick around to the end

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:09.680
of this video.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:17.740
Freaky is the new horror comedy from director
Christopher Landon, who is probably most known

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.470
for making the Happy Death Day movies.

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:23.300
This is kind of a perfect project for him,
because Happy Death Day is basically Groundhog

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:27.400
Day if it had a serial killer, and Freaky
is basically Freaky Friday if it had a serial

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:28.439
killer.

00:00:28.439 --> 00:00:30.930
"OK, so I was never the most popular."

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:31.930
"Homecoming's this weekend."

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:33.390
"Booker is gonna be at the dance."

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:35.190
"And boys never really noticed me."

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:36.190
Wait what?

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:37.290
I don't buy that for a second.

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:38.780
We're talking about Kathryn Newton here.

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:40.480
We're talking about Lucy Stephens herself.

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:41.670
She’s cute as hell.

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:45.760
Interesting fact by the way, her and the director
Christopher Landon are both alumni of the

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:47.750
Paranormal Activity franchise...

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:49.610
Yeah, you're right, that's not interesting.

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:53.290
But I do have to give the director points
implementing creative and creepy school mascots

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:54.290
in his movies.

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:56.370
Showing off a little bit of his directorial
trademark there.

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:58.510
And also having clever slogans for those teams.

00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:03.079
But the big homage here, other than Freaky
Friday and Happy Death Day is seen in this

00:01:03.079 --> 00:01:06.840
part, where the killer chases down the girl
with some kind of magically activated knife,

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:11.259
and suddenly stormy clouds and lightning fill
the skies as some kind of ritual is performed,

00:01:11.259 --> 00:01:14.999
the result of which is the killer's soul being
transferred into the girl and vice versa.

00:01:14.999 --> 00:01:18.999
The theatrics are almost exactly the same
as what's seen in Child's Play, which also

00:01:18.999 --> 00:01:23.539
features a serial killer using a ritual to
transfer his soul into another body, albeit

00:01:23.539 --> 00:01:24.959
a much stubbier one.

00:01:24.959 --> 00:01:28.600
In Child's Play, the killer discovers he has
a limited amount of time to transfer his soul

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:32.159
back into a human vessel before he gets stuck
inside the doll forever, and it seems like

00:01:32.159 --> 00:01:34.229
Freaky follows similar rules.

00:01:34.229 --> 00:01:38.499
"I have like less than six hours to swap back
or I'm gonna be stuck in this body forever."

00:01:38.499 --> 00:01:42.200
I also noticed that the killer, who is known
as the Blissview Butcher, wears a mask.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:46.049
It looks like a Redead Mask from The Legend
of Zelda: Ocarina of Time, which is closely

00:01:46.049 --> 00:01:49.740
related to something called the Gibdo Mask,
which allows you to blend in with Redeads

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:54.039
and Gibdos undetected, just as the Blissview
Butcher can blend in with his victims undetected

00:01:54.039 --> 00:01:55.649
while inside Millie's body.

00:01:55.649 --> 00:01:59.219
Maybe there will be a scene where she does
the same thing and uses her new body to slide

00:01:59.219 --> 00:02:03.639
in with criminals, just like Link uses various
masks to gain access to places in Majora's

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:04.140
Mask.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:07.060
It also bears a pretty close resemblance to
the Jason mask from Friday the 13th.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:11.090
In any event, even if that's not an intentional
reference, I do remember Christopher Landon

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:14.951
saying he wanted to bring back the idea of
the masked killer with Happy Death Day, and

00:02:14.951 --> 00:02:19.239
with that series potentially dead, no pun
intended, it's good to see him continuing

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:20.720
it in another form.

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:21.939
Pun intended that time.

00:02:21.939 --> 00:02:24.019
Cause Millie takes on another form...

00:02:24.019 --> 00:02:27.459
Don't know what's going on here, but yeah,
that's the end of the trailer.

00:02:27.459 --> 00:02:29.620
Friday the 13th because that's the spooky
day.

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:32.569
But let's be real, this things not gonna be
in theaters in November.

00:02:32.569 --> 00:02:35.989
My theory is that movie studios keep putting
release dates in the pandemic, because when

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:39.879
that date comes and they inevitably have to
delay it, people report on it and they get

00:02:39.879 --> 00:02:40.879
free press.

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:44.180
That being said, I wouldn't mind watching
this on my TV in November, but we'll see what

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:44.680
happens.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:47.640
Click the video on the left to see my Things You Missed episode on Happy Death Day,

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:50.980
If you love horror subscribe to this channel
right now.

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:51.980
I'm not asking.

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:56.140
I've got new horrors every week, so ring that
deathbell for notifications and I'll see you

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:59.260
in the next one, assuming we stay inside.

